{
  "version": 11,
  "randomSeed": "726e4ad6a66aad4a52a2265c3bfe7a42",
  "expressions": {
    "list": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "id": "8",
        "text": "The equation below has infinitely many solutions, where c and d are constants and c is positive. Find the value of c."
      },
      {
        "type": "expression",
        "id": "90",
        "hidden": true,
        "latex": "\\frac{48x+144}{8}-\\frac{c}{15}=d\\left(x-2\\right)"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "id": "9",
        "text": "For infinitely many solutions the coefficients of x must match, which fixes d."
      },
      {
        "type": "expression",
        "id": "91",
        "hidden": true,
        "latex": "d=\\frac{48}{8}"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "id": "92",
        "text": "Solving the constants for c gives the value below."
      },
      {
        "type": "expression",
        "id": "93",
        "hidden": true,
        "latex": "15\\left(\\frac{144}{8}+12\\right)"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "id": "11",
        "text": "A regression finds c once d is known. Regressing both constants at once gives a wrong value for c."
      },
      {
        "type": "expression",
        "id": "12",
        "color": "#2d70b3",
        "latex": "\\frac{\\left(48x_{1}+144\\right)}{8}-\\frac{c}{15}\\sim6\\left(x_{1}-2\\right)",
        "residualVariable": "e_{1}",
        "regressionParameters": {
          "x_{1}": 0,
          "c": 450
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "id": "94",
        "text": "The regression fitted value of c is the answer."
      }
    ]
  }
}
